  "executive_briefing": "Late 2026 intelligence indicates a pivotal dual evolution in the digital asset landscape: structural institutionalization alongside legislative formalization. Spot Bitcoin ETFs and treasury holdings (such as MicroStrategy's continued balance sheet expansions) have transitioned into standard institutional macro assets, reaching structural maturity. Concurrently, the advancing U.S. Digital Asset Market CLARITY Act in the Senate Banking Committee is establishing clear SEC-CFTC jurisdictional boundaries, removing regulatory opacity for institutional market participants. Technically, the BTC/ETH paradigm is defined by non-wrapped, trust-minimized native liquidity mechanisms like THORChain pools, while Bitcoin L2 execution models utilizing deterministic smart contract languages like Clarity continue to incubate as alternative security frameworks to EVM platforms. Ethereum remains the predominant, low-velocity enterprise settlement layer for DeFi.",
